  · tools/origin.js — Lyre's trail end to end, including that the directions
    actually point somewhere.
  · tools/raise.js  — the raise-mechanic rework: what the rite refuses (Watchers,
    machines) and what the rest comes back wearing. The shape assertions are
    measured off the built MESH, not off the flags, because carrying a flag no
    rig reads would pass a flag test and change nothing on screen.
  · tools/descend.js — the way into a cave and back out of it, driven through the
    same `orderFloor` the right-click handler calls.
  · tools/guns.js   — the turret, the emplaced lance and the handheld lance, each
    staged in the order a player actually meets it. The turret case is staged
    with the raid ALREADY under way, which is the only order that fails.
  · tools/roads.js  — fifteen caravans on the world's own routes for nine game-days,
    watching for wagons that stop moving. Nothing was fixed here; see the note.
  · tools/aid.js    — the squad bar's threat mark and cross-faction bandaging. Both
    are measured through the real surfaces: the mark off the rebuilt DOM, the
    bandage order through a real right-click on the canvas.

Two rules this file keeps learning the hard way, both worth reading first:
  1. A harness that passes on the broken build proves nothing. Several items
     below record a first assertion that did exactly that.
  2. Any new `ri()`/`rnd()` call at worldgen moves every body placed after it.
     Three separate harnesses have been broken by that one mechanism.
