[OPEN] Malathuun’s Curse: a world event, like the blood moon. A sundered site… stands up.
       (A carrion beast spawns somewhere in the world, not fully grown but not nascent either.)
    NOT STARTED, and almost all of the machinery is already sitting there waiting for it.
    `spawnCairnBeast(force)` ALREADY takes a force flag that skips the CAIRN_MAX check, and it
    ALREADY prefers to rise at a `corpseSites` entry — which is to say, at a sundered site.
    So the spawn half of this is one call.
    "Not fully grown but not nascent either" is a solved problem too: `c.ate` is the single
    number the whole stat line is computed from, and `cairnGrow(c)` recomputes big, blood,
    claw, tough, atk, pace and noise from it. Set `ate` to a mid value before calling
    `cairnGrow` and you get exactly the half-grown thing you are describing, with no new stats
    and nothing extra to save — the comment on `cairnGrow` says a save only has to store `ate`.
    The EVENT half is the part that does not exist. `worldEvent(kind, x, y, text)` is the entry
    point and there is already a `cairn:'bad'` tone registered for it. What a new kind needs is
    an entry in DREAD_WEIGHT (bloodmoon sits at 6, sundered at 10 — this probably wants to be
    heavier than both) and a line in each DREAD_TRAIT row, or leaders will have no opinion
    about it. A pious seat should care a great deal.
    Two things worth deciding before building: whether the site is CONSUMED (a sundered site
    that stood up should probably stop being lootable, and the loot-visibility item below is
    already about those sites), and whether the curse fires off the Fracture clock like the
    blood moon does or off something the player did. The second is more interesting — the
    Cairn Beast population already keys off unclaimed corpses, so the player's own
    housekeeping is an established dial for this creature and the curse could read the same one.

