    TWO REAL BUGS, both found by driving the descent:
      1. THE ONE-WAY TRIP. `onStair` is set the moment a body stands on a stair —
         including the tile it LANDS on, since a stair is one tile on both storeys —
         and `useStairs` tests it BEFORE it looks at `wantFloor`. So the flag outlived
         the order that set it: walk into a cave and every subsequent order to come
         back up is read and discarded, silently, forever. `orderFloor` and `routeTo`
         now clear it, because a new order is not a yo-yo.
      2. A STAIR EMBEDDED IN ROCK. `deck()` says "there is something to stand on"
         and says nothing about `blocked`, which the chamber ring wrote first. One
         down-stair in sixteen was decked, drawn and still solid — a level of the
         warren with no way down. New `carve()` clears both; the down-stair is also
         now placed strictly inside the room rather than up to 3 tiles off centre,
         and the landing is carved AFTER the side chambers, which could previously
         wall straight back over it.

